From 2b25912c6af5b3d3e60084b67c53dcaf033ee36c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doruk Aktun <info@dorukaktun.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:03:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Add SM8350 support

Add support for the Camera Subsystem found on the Qualcomm SM8350 SoC
(Titan 580).

The block is a close relative of the SM8250 (Titan 480) one: six
CSIPHYs, the CSID registers embedded in the VFE register regions at the
same offsets (0x1200 for a full VFE, 0x200 for a lite one), and a
VFE/CSID register layout handled by the existing VFE 480 and CSID gen2
code. SM8350 adds a third full CSID/VFE pair (IFE2), so it has three
full and two lite instances, like SC7280.

The CSIPHY is version 1.2.3, the same as on SM6350, so reuse the SM6350
lane configuration table.

With three full CSIDs the lite ones no longer start at index 2, so pick
the full or lite CSID offset inside the parent VFE region from the
is_lite flag of the resource table instead of from the CSID index. This
does not change SM8250, where CSID2 and CSID3 are the lite ones.

Clock rates and regulator loads come from the vendor device tree; the
VFE clock levels match the SM8350 camera clock controller frequency
tables.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
